# The reader Document must preserve both audiences

Slice A uses `/lore/services-capture-dependencies`. Its source has six bibliography entries, two glossary terms, internal links, and two pinned excerpts.

Decode the source through `parseLorePage` in `apps/mischief/scripts/content-lib.ts`. Do not replace structured `sources` and `terms` with strings.

## Inputs and authority

- Authored Brain content owns prose, bibliography, and terms.
- `packages/code-snippets` owns excerpt resolution and token output.
- The content generator owns heading and paragraph ids, citations, backlinks, and generation identity.
- One typed page descriptor owns route metadata. It includes source path, status, canonical policy, title, description, discovery links, robots, social image, and dates.
- The browser receives the complete document in Flags or initial Model. No initial Command fetches its body.

## Required Document shape

The one hand-converted page needs:

- Paragraphs containing text, code spans, links, paragraph anchors, and inbound counts.
- Headings with stable ids.
- Lists containing those same inline values.
- CodeSnippet nodes with source provenance, ranges, highlighted lines, and token data.
- A bibliography generated from decoded source records.
- Source/change metadata and linked-from entries generated by the existing graph.

Home additionally needs prompts, copy controls, diagrams, and tables. The shared shell owns nav, callout, agent pointer, breadcrumbs, and footer.

The later codemod must represent audience-specific blocks explicitly. Agent `read.text` cannot recover HumanOnly content. A rendered HTML string cannot recover a structured document safely.

## Migration boundary

This note describes the target. The hand-written Foldkit Document and its parity proof are still required.

The current preparation helper decodes the generated manifest/catalog, validates their generation, reads real HTML metadata, and decodes the selected lore frontmatter. Those old-renderer artifacts are comparison evidence. They must not become the replacement page's sole body implementation.

The initial route ledger covers 124 generated page paths and both HTML and Markdown representations. It is incomplete until special routes, aliases, redirects, and outcome/error statuses are added. Source paths for derived pages need explicit provenance.

No `@foldkit/markdown` pin is added for slice A. The content lane can use the verified shape when its dependency receives approval.

Related: [reader-site plan](./foldkit-site.svx).
